pi1s4-close-residual-hostile-review-sol56-20260831.md:87:   merely `CHECKED` on examples, then later uses it in the `PROVED-HERE` degree-seven claim.  For a singular branch it is true.  A short induction supplies the missing proof: after one tangent blow-up, if `beta_1-m>=m`, the new pair is `(m,beta_h-m)`; otherwise, after swapping coordinates, it is `(beta_1-m,beta_h-beta_1+m)`.  Adding the current centre's multiplicity `m` preserves `m+beta_h-1` in both cases.  At the terminal smooth tangent state `(1,k)`, the `k` multiplicity-one centres give `1+k-1`.  Thus (4.2) may be promoted only with this proof inserted.
