pi1s4-close-residual-hostile-review-sol56-20260831.md:108:   Thus `C[p,q]=C[t^3,t^4+t]`, its fraction field is `C(t)`, and its degree semigroup is `<3,4>`, with gaps `1,2,5`.  The degree-six curve has `delta_aff=3`, hence `delta_inf=7`, `beta_1=15`, and `M_inf=16>15`.  It has an ordinary triple point over `t^3=-1`, so it is not a residual `D_1`; it refutes the semigroup inference and the unrestricted `(6,4)` claim, while leaving the double-point residual case OPEN.  In that case the needed target is only `delta_aff>=4` (`beta_1<=13`), not the report's unsupported `>=5`.
