   259	Every escaping residual must satisfy gcd(d,n)=g>=2, reduced pair
   260	(d/g,n/g) in (u,1), (odd u,2), or (4,3), and
   261	g <= gcd(deg P,deg Q)-2.
   262	
   263	d = 2g_L + c(Pi) + 2, where g_L is the compact genus of a generic restricted
   264	degree-four cover over a target line and c(Pi) is the number of cycles of the
   265	infinity permutation.
   266	
   267	Through d<=9 the noncoprime Chau list is
   268	(4,2); (6,2),(6,3),(6,4); (8,2),(8,4),(8,6); (9,3),(9,6).
   269	
   270	The promoted coprime intermediate survivor table is Chau-filtered to (4,3).
